  "input": "task: semantic similarity between historical scouting games\noriginal-language: en\noriginal-title: The Man-Hunt\noriginal-context: This is played with a scout and ten or more hostiles, or hounds, according to the country, more when it is rough or wooded. The scout is given a letter addressed to the \"Military Commandant\" (usually the lady of the house that he gets to) of any given place a mile or two away. He is told to take the letter to anyone of three given houses, and get it endorsed, with the hour when he arrived, then return to the starting-point within a certain time. The hostiles are sent to a point half-way, and let go by a starter at the same time as the scout leaves the camp. They are to intercept him. If they catch him before he delivers the letter he must ransom his life by paying each two arrow heads (or other forfeit) and his captor keeps the letter as a trophy. If he gets through, but is caught on the road back, he pays half as much for his life. If he gets through, but is over time, it is a draw. If he gets through successfully on time he claims three arrow heads from each hostile and keeps the letter as a trophy. They may not follow him into the house (that is, the fort), but may surround it at one hundred yards distance. They do not know which three houses he is free to enter, but they do know that these are within certain limits. The scout should wear a conspicuous badge (hat, shirt, coat, or feather), and may ride a wheel or go in a wagon, etc., as long as his badge is clearly visible. To \"tag\" the scout is not to capture. \"The blockade to be binding must be effectual.\"\nparallel-language: pl\nparallel-title: Polowanie na człowieka\nparallel-context: Gra ta jest rozgrywana z jednym harcerzem i dziesięcioma lub więcej przeciwnikami, czyli ogarami, w zależności od terenu – więcej, gdy jest on nierówny lub zalesiony. Harcerz otrzymuje list zaadresowany do „Komendanta Wojskowego” (zazwyczaj pani domu, do której ma dotrzeć) w dowolnym miejscu oddalonym o jedną lub dwie mile. Ma on dostarczyć list do jednej z trzech wskazanych posesji, uzyskać jego potwierdzenie z godziną przybycia, a następnie wrócić do punktu wyjścia w określonym czasie. Przeciwnicy są wysyłani do punktu w połowie drogi i wypuszczani przez startera w tym samym czasie, w którym harcerz opuszcza obóz. Ich zadaniem jest przechwycenie go. Jeśli złapią go przed dostarczeniem listu, musi wykupić swoje życie, płacąc każdemu po dwie groty strzał (lub inną karę), a schwytujący zatr",
